  "body": "Package maintainers can now let their package manager handle app updates and setup.\n\nBuild from the source folder with both options:\n\n```sh\nbuildinfo=github.com/Watchdog0x/jabridge/internal/buildinfo\nCGO_ENABLED=0 go build -buildvcs=false -o jabridge -ldflags \"\\\n-X ${buildinfo}.SelfUpdate=disabled \\\n-X ${buildinfo}.Setup=disabled\" ./cmd/jabridge\n```\n\nYour package must install the USB rules and user service from `internal/assets`. Point the service at the packaged app with `--daemon`, and start it before opening the menu. [Package setup steps](https://github.com/Watchdog0x/jabridge/blob/main/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md#package-managed-builds).\n\nThe menu can use the packaged service even when history cannot be saved. Testing on NixOS itself is still needed.\n\nFor official downloads, update with:\n\n```sh\njabridge update\n```\n\nThanks @rclement for #51 and #52.\n",
